    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`, and `pytest -q` passes. The only existing test checks that the labels are lowercase, so the new function has no test of its own and I haven't called the real API.\n\nWhat it does:\n\n- **One request:** a single call to the Messages API with `model=MODEL` (`claude-sonnet-4-6`), `max_tokens=5` and `temperature=0`.\n- **Prompts:** the system prompt is built from `LABELS`: \"Classify the support ticket. Answer with exactly one word from this list: bug, feature, question.\" The ticket text is sent as the only user message.\n- **Result:** it joins the reply's text, strips it and lower-cases it. If the result is one of `LABELS` it's returned; otherwise the function returns `\"question\"`. It reads the reply the same way `app/summaries.py` does.\n\n`temperature=0` works on `claude-sonnet-4-6`, but the API rejects it with an error on newer models (Sonnet 5, Opus 4.7 and later, Fable 5). `app/summaries.py` imports `MODEL` from the labeler, so if `MODEL` is changed to one of those models, `label_ticket` will start failing. Even at temperature 0, the model's output isn't guaranteed to be identical every time. The fallback to `\"question\"` keeps the return value always within `LABELS`.\n\nNo dependencies were added."
  },
